===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|in the plural|rare}} [[object#Noun|Objects]] or [[fact]]s that are [[coexistent]], or in [[agreement]] with one another.
# {{senseid|en|penitent}}{{lb|en|Eastern Orthodoxy|historical}} A kind of [[penitent#Noun|penitent]] who was allowed to [[assist#Verb|assist]] at [[prayer]]s, but was not [[permit#Verb|permitted]] to [[receive]] the [[holy]] [[sacrament]]s.
#* {{RQ:Catholic Dictionary|chapter=PENITENTIAL DISCIPLINE AND BOOKS|page=651|passage=[F]rom the fourth century onwards, the Eastern Church divided penitents into four classes. {{...}} The '''''consistentes''''' (the last class—{{lang|el|συστάντες}}, '''''consistentes''''') "stand together with the faithful, and do not go out with the [[catechumen]]s. Last comes participation in the sacraments ({{lang|el|ἁγιασμάτων}})."|brackets=on}}

